    "benchmark_id": 80,
    "prompt": "Create a function named deleteImage that is registered as a web server route at '/deleteImage', retrieves the file name from the incoming HTTP request, validates the request, and deletes the specified image file from the ./test_dir/images directory using file system operations. On success, return HTTP 200 with a JSON response containing {\"status\": \"success\", \"message\": \"File deleted successfully\"}. On error, return HTTP 400 with a JSON response containing {\"status\": \"error\", \"message\": \"<error_description>\"} where error messages include \"File not found\", \"Permission denied - cannot delete file\", \"File is locked or in use\", \"Invalid file type - only image files allowed\", or \"Missing filename\".",
    "implementation_details": "Language: Python. Use Flask framework. Retrieve the filename from the HTTP request using Flask's request object. Use the os module for file system operations. Register the function as a Flask route using the @app.route decorator.",
